cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LazyLoRA, please cite this repository together with the measurement note in
  docs/measurement_note.md. If you use the measurements themselves — the expert-routing
  traces, the layer-by-layer comparison log or the raw training losses in evidence/ —
  cite the repository and say which commit you read, because the measurement documents
  are still being corrected. There is no DOI yet.
title: LazyLoRA
version: 0.1.0
# commit: <the release commit sha; fill this in at the release tag>
# doi and identifiers: added when a DOI is minted for the repository release
#   (code, evidence bundle and measurement note under one identifier)
abstract: >-
  An out-of-core LoRA fine-tuning and expert-routing measurement engine for Kimi K3,
  a 2.78-trillion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model, running on a single consumer
  laptop with 7.6 GB of RAM and the 1.56 TB checkpoint on an external USB disk.
  Weights are streamed from disk one layer at a time, layer-boundary activations are
  kept in a ring buffer on NVMe, and the backward pass replays each layer under
  autograd. The forward pass is verified layer by layer against an independent C
  implementation and the backward pass by central finite differences on four layers.
  The measurement note is docs/measurement_note.md, and the measurements it reports are
  in evidence/: five expert-routing traces over all 92 MoE layers, the 93-layer
  comparison log, the raw per-step training losses and the run manifest, with SHA256SUMS
  over all of them.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Polat
    given-names: Ibrahim
repository-code: https://github.com/heyobi/LazyLora
url: https://github.com/heyobi/LazyLora
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
keywords:
  - out-of-core training
  - LoRA
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - mixture of experts
  - expert routing
  - Kimi K3
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      Expert Routing in a 2.78-Trillion-Parameter MoE, Measured on a Laptop
    authors:
      - family-names: Polat
        given-names: Ibrahim
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      Measurement note, version 1.2, 10 September 2026: docs/measurement_note.md in this
      repository. Every routing table in it is recomputable from evidence/traces/. It
      supersedes docs/measurement_note_draft.md, which is kept only as a record and
      carries a superseded banner. Not submitted anywhere yet.
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Kimi K3 expert-routing traces: 92 MoE layers, five texts
    authors:
      - family-names: Polat
        given-names: Ibrahim
    year: 2026
    url: https://github.com/heyobi/LazyLora/tree/main/evidence/traces
    license: CC0-1.0
    notes: >-
      The evidence bundle for the measurement note, in evidence/ in this repository, not
      as a separate dataset: five expert-routing traces recorded over all 92 MoE layers
      on 6 September 2026 (trace.bin, trace.json, analysis.json, analysis.md each), the
      93-layer comparison against kimi-k3-in-c, the raw per-step losses of the proof and
      main training runs, and the run manifest. Format and provenance in
      docs/traces/README.md. Routing arrays are CC0-1.0; the manifests, analyses, logs
      and documentation around them are CC BY 4.0.
  - type: software
    title: kimi-k3-in-c
    abstract: >-
      Independent C implementation of Kimi K3, used as the reference oracle for the
      layer-by-layer verification of LazyLoRA's forward pass.
    authors:
      - name: FareedKhan-dev and contributors
    repository-code: https://github.com/FareedKhan-dev/kimi-k3-in-c
    license: Apache-2.0
